{"term":"convey","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:8eef80d8423d2e81c2","definition":"To move (something) from one place to another.","example":"Air conveys sound. Water is conveyed through the pipe.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["carry","transport","port"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["conveyability","conveyable","conveyal","conveyance","conveyee","conveyer","conveyor","misconvey","preconvey","reconvey","unconveyable","unconveyed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convey#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2ba4f6a32212ae3b99","definition":"To take or carry (someone) from one place to another.","example":"Convey me to my bed, then to my grave:\nLove they to live that love and honour have.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["accompany","conduct","escort"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["conveyability","conveyable","conveyal","conveyance","conveyee","conveyer","conveyor","misconvey","preconvey","reconvey","unconveyable","unconveyed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convey#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fbc124773fc06469e7","definition":"To communicate; to make known; to portray.","example":"to convey an impression; to convey information","pos":"verb","synonyms":["express","send","relay","impart"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["conveyability","conveyable","conveyal","conveyance","conveyee","conveyer","conveyor","misconvey","preconvey","reconvey","unconveyable","unconveyed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convey#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c344fe9cdea7458daf","definition":"To transfer legal rights (to).","example":"He conveyed ownership of the company to his daughter.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["accompany","conduct","escort"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["conveyability","conveyable","conveyal","conveyance","conveyee","conveyer","conveyor","misconvey","preconvey","reconvey","unconveyable","unconveyed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convey#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b9e28dfbdd83e379f3","definition":"To manage with privacy; to carry out.","example":"1557, uncredited translator, A Mery Dialogue by Erasmus, London: Antony Kytson,\nI shall so conuey my matters, that he shall dysclose all together hym selfe, what busynesse is betwene you […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["accompany","conduct","escort"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["conveyability","conveyable","conveyal","conveyance","conveyee","conveyer","conveyor","misconvey","preconvey","reconvey","unconveyable","unconveyed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convey#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:38d35e06da87ee32d1","definition":"To carry or take away secretly; to steal; to thieve.","example":"Suppose you are good at the lift, who be more cunning then we women, in that we are more trusted, for they little suspect vs, and we haue as close conueyance as you men, though you haue Cloakes, we haue skirts of gownes, handbaskets, the crownes of our hattes, our plackardes, and for a need, false bagges vnder our smockes, wherein we can conuey more closely then you.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["accompany","conduct","escort"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["conveyability","conveyable","conveyal","conveyance","conveyee","conveyer","conveyor